WEBVTT

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.650
What were you trying to do?

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.000
What Kunagisa was about to do was, in the long run, illegal.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.640
In short, she was gathering data.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.500
Kanami included, there were twelve people staying here.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.980
Minus myself and Kunagisa, ten.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.680
She was looking for any contact between them before coming here.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.170
Kunagisa Tomo's Attendant

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.160
So? How's this work?

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.380
cover this all up argh

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.380
one more I guess

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.380
Kunagisa Tomo

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.380
Genius Engineer

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:34.380
First, I access the high-spec machine I got at home.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.280
Then get in touch with Chee-kun.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:41.160
Chee-kun? That's a new name.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:45.920
Chee-kun's main role was being our Seeker.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:51.400
Chee-kun can find out about anything in the galaxy!

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:53.540
...the galaxy?

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:02.540
What I lack is everything you have

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:09.670
What I want to be is everything you want

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:13.260
The moment we first met

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.800
I'm sure I already knew

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.140
Even before it began

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:24.890
Behind my words

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:27.900
I'm always hiding

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:33.150
Keeping my feelings buried deep

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:47.080
Now, the world that keeps us trapped sure changes before you know it

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:56.260
I mean my heart's already dyed a single color,
in my mind the answer's already been chosen

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:02.720
Is it fate? I don't know, but I'll reach out my hand

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:06.430
I bet we don't need words at all

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:10.310
Your melody and my rhythm

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:14.900
Clamp up our feelings and spin out our fingers

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.240
I'll always be right here

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:24.120
<i>The Beheading Cycle</i>

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:24.120
<i>The Blue Savant and
the Master of Nonsense</i>

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:22.120
Right by your side

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:24.120
<i>Day 4 (2) The 0.14 Tragedy</i>

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.120
<i>The Beheading Cycle</i>

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:27.500
Spiral Staircase Room - Left

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.750
1st Floor, Center Hall

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.040
1st Floor, Akagami Ilia's Room, Exterior

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:32.040
Yes?

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.210
1st Floor, Akagami Ilia's Room

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.210
Cover this

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.210
Uhh

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.210
Mansion's Head Maid

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.210
Wet Wing Raven
Island's Owner

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.210
Handa Rei

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.210
Akagami Ilia

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:35.740
What is it?

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:40.120
I was hoping to talk with you a little, Ilia.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.120
Very well. Please, sit.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:50.060
I was up all night, and I'm rather tired.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:56.680
I was about to retire. If we could make this brief...

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:03.360
Ilia, why won't you call the police?

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:07.700
I believe I explained that already.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:13.080
If we called the police, they would assume Sonoyama was the killer.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.080
But how is that different from our current situation?

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.620
We've already imprisoned her.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:25.860
Ilia, what we're doing is illegal.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.640
So what?

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:36.360
The people I invite here matter to the world.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.140
I refuse to allow them to be fed on by the brutish authorities.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.980
No one enjoys being suspected of something they did not do.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:45.400
And...

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.900
No matter who the killer is...

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:52.200
I have no intention of casting them to the mercy of the law.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:56.680
If it takes the full might of the Akagami Foundation...I'll protect them.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:58.260
Why?

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.920
Geniuses are not equal under the law.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:08.580
I can't help but feel like you have
some other reason for not calling the police.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:12.980
So...are you finished?

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.880
I am very sleepy.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:18.980
Pardon me.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:20.660
I will walk you back.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:31.920
Please don't take anything she says to heart.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:32.370
1st Floor, Living Room

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.200
She's never been very good at tact.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:36.540
Oh.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.520
I didn't plan on it.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:44.340
Truth is, she simply really admires Aikawa.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:49.020
That, I believe, is why she doesn't want to call the police.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:55.220
I'm sure Miss Ilia sees this as a welcoming present.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:59.320
Aikawa has the right personality for cases like this.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.620
I do beg your pardon.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:10.780
Rei seemed much nicer than I imagined.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:12.600
I was rather taken aback.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:18.020
Hikari had made her sound like a very demanding individual.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.050
2nd Floor, Kunagisa Tomo's Room

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:29.050
Cover all this up

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:29.050
Genius Fortune Teller

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:29.050
Himena Maki

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:41.360
2nd Floor, Kunagisa Tomo's Room, Exterior

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.500
You are very careless.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:49.180
Or maybe just thoughtless?

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:51.980
What are you talking about?

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:56.700
Leaving Kunagisa alone in her room.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:01.140
If I'd turned out to be the killer, what then?

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.340
If you really value someone...

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:08.720
Never take your eyes often them.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:11.400
Remember that, my boy.

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:27.110
Absent

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:26.700
Akari and Teruko are...?

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:31.120
They've gone to the mainland to get in touch with Aikawa.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:33.480
You can't just call, or e-mail?

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:34.980
No.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:38.960
1st Floor, Dining Room

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.880
Aikawa is notoriously hard to contact.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.800
Far too much work to do.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:45.880
So they won't be back until tomorrow.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:47.900
Too much work?

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:51.860
What kind of work, exactly?

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.440
Aikawa's a consultant.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.220
Tell me, Kunagisa...

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:03.520
You were engaged in some furtive activities
this afternoon, right? Figure anything out?

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:06.220
I've figured everything out!

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:11.420
So many things it takes aaaages to figure out which to do.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:12.980
Himena.

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:14.160
What say you?

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:18.740
Will you tell us how things will turn out?

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:20.080
It'll cost you.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:26.020
She's living here for free, but digging for more?

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:31.000
How horribly greedy could anyone be? Like the devil incarnate.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.900
I hardly deserve that.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:35.390
Protective
Custody

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:37.860
I'd be happy to pay.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:39.920
Please, proceed.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:41.080
It'll be over soon.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.300
Is that it?

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:53.920
I have to say...

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:55.820
That was free.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:59.520
A certain someone wouldn't shut up about it.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.900
So I tossed that one out there.

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:07.340
Pay it no attention. It has nothing to do with the point of anything.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:12.930
Ibuki Kanami's
Assistant

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:12.930
Genius Chef

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.720
Oh...OK. I get it.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:25.640
How could that have happened?

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.480
It doesn't make any sense.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:33.860
An artist of Kanami's caliber would never make such an obvious mistake.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:40.400
Uh...hey, Hikari.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:43.000
Er...come in.

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:44.800
Thank you.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:51.260
Um, is Tomo here?

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:53.440
Oh, Kunagisa?

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:58.180
I bound her hand and foot and tossed her in the bath.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:00.800
She's like a cat.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:02.560
Hates baths.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:11.420
Her hair is naturally a much lighter shade of blue,
you know. But she never washes it, and it usually looks darker.

00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:18.500
She's not much of an escape artist, and once she gets wet,
she gives up and always winds up taking a very long soak.

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:26.700
Um. So. If you need to talk to her, it'll have to wait.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:28.660
Wait...

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:31.340
Hikari, do you have time right now?

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:36.860
Mm? Well, yes...I've finished work for the day.

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:39.560
Then do you mind waiting here?

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:43.340
I don't want to leave Kunagisa alone.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.720
I don't mind, but...

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.880
Of course, I'd be happy to.

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:53.720
But are you sure you want to leave me with her?

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:56.980
I doubt anyone would attack when there's two of you here.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:00.860
No, I mean...if you want her safe...

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:02.360
Not a problem.

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:08.840
Maki, maybe. But I trust you.

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:14.780
Yeesh. 'I trust you'?

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:18.760
Spiral Staircase Room - Right

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:24.800
When? When had I become capable of using a word like that?

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:26.800
This is me, here.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.780
Q: What does 'trust' mean?

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:34.020
A: You don't mind being betrayed.

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:36.940
You won't regret it when you are.

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:42.320
Nonsense either way.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.540
1st Floor, Storeroom, Exterior

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:50.540
It's me.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:52.500
Oh?

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:55.640
Well...I've been thinking about it.

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:59.040
And I wanted to apologize to you.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:02.600
Why on earth would you do that?

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:05.340
You protected me.

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:11.760
I should be thanking you. That's all.

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:14.780
I could have suggested it myself.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.440
But I figured that was a bad idea.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:22.280
When you suggested it for me, I was grateful.

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:25.300
I should put that gratitude in words.

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:27.200
Thank you.

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:30.080
You're welcome.

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:34.820
So, I hear you've been poking around.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:38.800
Can you tell me what you've found out?

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.820
<i>I</i> don't know the killer yet.

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:44.560
<i>You</i> don't? Hmm.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:48.300
That sounds significant. I do like weighted statements.

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:51.280
Okay, so let me change the question.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:55.020
How goes your thoughts on the locked room?

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:57.300
What do you make of it, Akane?

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.280
It's a post hoc fallacy.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:02.080
Is that English?

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:03.620
It's Latin.

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:11.180
Latin. I dunno the Japanese. Like blaming the rooster for the sunrise.

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:13.580
Oh. Yeah.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:17.640
She's already figured the locked room out.

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:24.200
She solved it, but she agreed to be locked up
to prevent anything else happening.

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:26.900
She really is impressive.

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:32.140
Ilia's favorite is arriving soon.

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:38.020
Maintaining the status quo till this Aikawa
gets here seemed like the best plan.

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:42.640
Do you know who the killer is, too?

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:44.260
That, I don't know.

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:46.440
Cross my heart and hope to die.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:49.960
Hardly my field.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:54.920
I've read a few mystery novels, but just for fun, you know?

00:12:57.180 --> 00:13:00.000
You ever read Mushanokoji Saneatsu?

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:02.760
Extracts, at least.

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:05.760
Then you know Shinri Sensei вЂ“ the Teacher of Truth?

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:06.960
That much, sure.

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:13.980
Anyway, early in the book, the teacher of truth
talks about why it's bad to kill people.

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:15.980
You remember it?

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:17.100
Yes.

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:24.020
'Would you ever agree to let someone kill you? What
conditions would make your murder acceptable? Please, tell me.'

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:30.780
'If you would never consent to your murder,
then surely it is never permissible to kill another.'

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:31.620
Right?

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:33.540
Exactly.

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:38.160
So let me ask you that same question.

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:42.660
Would you ever agree to let someone kill you?

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:44.100
No.

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:49.680
If it were a choice between your life or Kunagisa's, what would you do?

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:51.940
I don't want to think about it.

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:53.180
Of course not.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:57.200
That's the way you are, right?

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:03.580
You despise having to choose. You do not
accept that you have to make a choice.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:09.600
Himena said something similar yesterday, but
she really hit the nail on the head, didn't she?

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:14.540
You just let yourself drift. Avoiding conflict.

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:19.340
Never clarifying anything. You're an ambiguist.

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:21.260
I don't deny it.

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:24.710
You don't deny it, but you won't admit it either.

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:28.220
You hate people?

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:29.460
Not really.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:30.920
Do you like them?

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.180
That's certainly not true.

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:40.320
Right. The base line for your value system
is the belief that people are better off alone.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:41.640
Belief...or desire.

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:45.600
The desire to make that notion true defines you.

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:50.280
All hyperbole aside, you really do prefer to be alone.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:55.580
Well, yeah. I am my oldest friend.

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:57.060
Aren't we all?

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:02.320
The self is the best friend any of us will ever have.

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:05.180
So what does that make Kunagisa?

00:15:05.740 --> 00:15:11.080
Add up your time together, and you've
not know each other long. Less than a year.

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:15.340
Are you in love with her?

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:19.180
No. Nothing like that.

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:21.480
Hmph. Okay.

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:27.380
But Kunagisa loves you. I'm sure of that.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:31.260
Probably. She's said as much.

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:35.120
She likes everyone.

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:37.560
Genuinely, everyone.

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:43.740
There's no reason why it needs to be me by her side.

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:49.480
Ah ha. You don't want Kunagisa to
love you. That's not what you're after.

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:52.620
You want her to<i> choose</i> you.

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:55.320
You and you alone.

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:03.140
But why Kunagisa? That's what I don't understand.

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:07.260
Yet I feel like there's a clear reason, somewhere.

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:12.240
People like you normally can't stand dating someone like her вЂ“

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:20.240
a partner that is superior to you, but less mature. Especially men like you.

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.520
I enjoy being with her.

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:25.260
No, that's not right...

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:27.320
Not quite...

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:33.620
Yeah...I enjoy being next to her.

00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:38.980
Then you're a bit of a masochist.

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:41.760
I was bullied in elementary school.

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:44.260
I certainly lean that way.

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:47.420
You were bullied? That's not right.

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:50.280
You were more likely ostracized.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:57.660
Rejection and abuse are not the same thing. Children
torture liars and the weak, and avoid those that don't fit in.

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:01.700
Equality, for better or worse.

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:04.440
Just round pi down to three.

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:10.040
Seemed like the other six Seven Fools had similar experiences.

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:12.980
The .14 tragedy.

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:15.820
Genius is born from not fitting in.

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:20.360
But not all who don't fit in becomes geniuses.

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:29.640
I believe you're intelligent enough to grasp the difference
between a warning and coercion, so let me offer a kindly warning.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:35.540
If you want Kunagisa to choose you, I suggest taking her to bed.

00:17:36.060 --> 00:17:39.800
That'll make you her one and only.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:42.560
I'm sure she won't resist.

00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:48.840
You may be an introverted gloomy little twisted ingrate
oblivious to adolescent rebellion and hormones,

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:52.840
but you've still got it in you to do that much.

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:55.240
I really don't.

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:58.600
Um, back to the first question...

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:00.500
Mm? What?

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:06.560
What about you, Akane? Would you ever be willing
to let someone kill you? Even for a moment?

00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:13.060
A moment? A moment!? I am always ready.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:16.320
'When it is time to die, then it is good to die.'

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:28.220
I, Sonoyama Akane, have no complaints, no matter
when, where, how, or who by I shall be murdered.

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:22.830
Cover me up

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:22.830
Sonoyama Akane

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:22.830
Genius - Seven Fools

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.860
Ii-chaaaan! Welcome baaack!

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:38.320
Ii-chan! I washed my hair, see! Praise me, praise me!

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:42.220
Looks cute.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:48.480
What brought you here, Hikari?

00:18:48.740 --> 00:18:55.580
Oh, right. Miss Ilia had something she absolutely
wanted me to ask you. The locked room trick.

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:59.760
She said she was sure you'd figured it out.

00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:03.140
We're not trying to be coy.

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:08.640
It's a simple trick; anyone who reads enough
mystery novels would see right through it.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:14.240
But when you see it for real, it's a different story.

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:19.120
The smell of blood, the presence of death...it drowns you.

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:23.260
Ii-chan! Such purple prose!

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.260
So silly!

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:27.360
Um...Tomo.

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:32.340
So, Tomo, if you do understand, than could you tell me?

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:38.640
Sure thing! But only if you answer my question in return.

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:44.160
First, let us review the scene!

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:48.160
Tah-dah! The studio!

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:51.320
The problem...is this paint.

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:58.420
The earthquake happened at one, the
shelves toppled over, and this is the result.

00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:04.960
If Kanami was murdered after the earthquake,
then how did the killer get in and out?

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.020
Still with me?

00:20:07.540 --> 00:20:08.840
Yes, so far.

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:15.880
Then the natural conclusion is that the murder
must have happened before the earthquake.

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:20.480
But Shinya spoke to Kanami on the phone after the earthquake.

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:23.820
So, Hikari. What now?

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:25.640
I have no idea.

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:32.000
For example, Hikari вЂ“ here is a hundred yen coin.

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:36.680
I say, 'It'll be heads', OK?

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:39.300
And then...I flip it.

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:44.220
Golly! It's heads.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:48.420
What do you think? You think it's a coincidence, right?

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:50.800
Normal reaction!

00:20:51.320 --> 00:20:54.320
But some people might draw the wrong conclusion.

00:20:54.320 --> 00:21:04.200
They would assume the coin was heads <i>because</i> I said it
would be. They would imagine me to have psychic powers.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:09.940
But that's not true, Hikari.

00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:17.840
In other words, Hikari, because B happened
after A does not mean that A caused B.

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:22.960
Which brings us to the question, Hikari.

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:30.080
There was an earthquake...and a river of paint.
But are these two things actually related?

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:32.520
Oh, I see!

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:37.760
You mean the earthquake <i>didn't</i> make that river?

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:47.320
The shelves probably did fall over. But I doubt the
spill was anything like as crazy large as that river.

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:50.980
Okay, I think I get the rest.

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:58.680
So the killer came in after the earthquake, and murdered Ibuki.

00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:08.520
Then, on their way out, they deliberately made the
spill larger. Carefully, so as not to leave any footprints.

00:22:09.180 --> 00:22:11.120
Right?

00:22:11.120 --> 00:22:16.300
Yes. And that gives us a <i>lot</i> more suspects.

00:22:16.500 --> 00:22:21.440
Then there's no reason to keep Akane locked up, is there?

00:22:22.200 --> 00:22:27.020
Akane already figured out the locked room trick.

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:32.000
And she pretended not to.

00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:38.340
Why? That makes no sense. Why would she do that?

00:22:38.800 --> 00:22:41.260
To keep things from escalating.

00:22:41.900 --> 00:22:44.680
She's very, very smart.

00:22:45.160 --> 00:22:48.880
Then we should probably keep this secret.

00:22:49.220 --> 00:22:51.840
Until we know who the killer is.

00:22:52.460 --> 00:22:57.060
I think confusing the situation is risky.

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:02.120
Now then, Hikari! My turn to ask a question!

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:06.820
Uh, oh, right. I did promise.

00:23:07.900 --> 00:23:10.380
Go ahead, ask away.

00:23:10.600 --> 00:23:12.860
Why is Ilia here?

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:16.860
Um. Well...

00:23:17.600 --> 00:23:20.860
I...well...um...

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:23.640
You won't answer, Hikari?

00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:27.760
I can't...not that. Sorry, Tomo.

00:23:28.080 --> 00:23:30.760
I'll answer anything but that.

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:34.560
Never mind then.

00:23:35.340 --> 00:23:38.860
Tomo, drop it, okay?

00:23:41.200 --> 00:23:46.060
Okay, Ii-chan. Not much else I can do.

00:23:46.260 --> 00:23:48.080
Sorry, Hikari.

00:23:48.480 --> 00:23:53.480
No, I mean...you answered all my questions, and I...

00:24:05.460 --> 00:24:06.960
From Chee-kun!

00:24:07.480 --> 00:24:09.980
He works fast!

00:24:09.980 --> 00:24:14.580
They say he ignores the Theory of Relativity
the way the rest of us do traffic signals.

00:24:16.060 --> 00:24:19.860
Hey, Ii-chan. He found a connection.

00:24:20.680 --> 00:24:26.480
Ibuki Kanami and Sonoyama Akane ate together at a cafe in Chicago.

00:24:27.100 --> 00:24:30.280
So he says. About six months ago.

00:24:33.100 --> 00:24:35.900
They ate together!? Why!?

00:24:36.440 --> 00:24:40.280
Didn't they hate each other?

00:24:40.780 --> 00:24:43.560
We'd been right. There was a connection.

00:24:44.500 --> 00:24:47.600
But why Akane and Kanami?

00:25:01.660 --> 00:25:04.260
Ii-chan, let's sleep together!

00:25:04.380 --> 00:25:05.260
No.

00:25:05.500 --> 00:25:09.640
Nights are still cold. You'll get sick sleeping there!

00:25:10.060 --> 00:25:13.540
This bed's king size, plenty of room.

00:25:13.780 --> 00:25:14.400
No.

00:25:14.700 --> 00:25:18.620
I promise I won't do anything! Just sleeping. Nothing else!

00:25:19.180 --> 00:25:22.280
I won't even touch you. We can put our backs to each other!

00:25:22.520 --> 00:25:24.040
You're in, right?

00:25:25.140 --> 00:25:25.920
No.

00:25:26.160 --> 00:25:28.660
Please. I'm so lonely.

00:25:34.800 --> 00:25:36.620
You promise not to do anything?

00:25:41.180 --> 00:25:44.020
Promise? I'm trusting you here.

00:25:44.020 --> 00:25:47.440
Don't worry, I'll never betray you!

00:26:01.160 --> 00:26:02.140
Ii-chan!

00:26:23.180 --> 00:26:28.920
If you want Kunagisa to choose you, I suggest taking her to bed.

00:26:29.160 --> 00:26:32.660
That'll make you her one and only.

00:26:34.820 --> 00:26:36.420
Nonsense.

00:26:37.900 --> 00:26:38.660
If...

00:26:40.020 --> 00:26:40.780
If...

00:26:42.140 --> 00:26:44.860
I'd said I'd already done that...

00:26:46.020 --> 00:26:48.520
Would Akane have despised me for it?

00:26:49.840 --> 00:26:53.700
And not with love in mind...but with destruction.

00:26:58.380 --> 00:26:59.960
But, Akane...

00:27:01.240 --> 00:27:03.880
There was no point to it at all.

00:27:05.360 --> 00:27:06.300
Really.

00:27:07.840 --> 00:27:10.060
No point at all.

00:27:12.180 --> 00:27:12.940
So...

00:27:13.840 --> 00:27:17.180
So what am I supposed to do?

00:27:18.380 --> 00:27:19.600
Tell me.

00:27:31.870 --> 00:27:37.340
The shape of the world I'd believed in

00:27:37.340 --> 00:27:40.760
Spun around when near you

00:27:40.930 --> 00:27:44.140
Leaning towards your right

00:27:44.140 --> 00:27:46.600
What I've got in my hands

00:27:46.600 --> 00:27:49.480
Is not a dream or nothing

00:27:49.480 --> 00:27:53.150
But there's something somewhere

00:27:53.150 --> 00:27:56.190
Throbbing in my heart

00:27:56.190 --> 00:27:59.110
If the one that you do love

00:27:59.110 --> 00:28:03.450
Agrees to put his arms around you

00:28:03.450 --> 00:28:06.200
Then what was a nebulous hope

00:28:06.200 --> 00:28:10.460
Shatters everything that kept you stable

00:28:10.460 --> 00:28:13.040
We'd once been so hollow

00:28:13.040 --> 00:28:15.880
Trapped inside that little box

00:28:15.880 --> 00:28:19.380
But now we've seen outside that box

00:28:19.380 --> 00:28:22.630
And have no idea where we are.

00:28:23.050 --> 00:28:24.470
That's all.

00:28:38.360 --> 00:28:40.860
Afterimages of our bliss

00:28:40.860 --> 00:28:43.700
Glimpses of the future

00:28:43.700 --> 00:28:47.280
A glance at something fragile

00:28:47.280 --> 00:28:52.120
Those times that we can still laugh together
